00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:19.631
-Even-- I--
-ROB: Yes.

00:03:19.698 --> 00:03:20.934
Not just the funniest kid.

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:22.735
He thought
he was the funniest person--

00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:25.171
I mean, Albert at 16
was a prodigy.

00:03:25.237 --> 00:03:27.239
He could make my dad,
Mel Brooks,

00:03:27.306 --> 00:03:29.375
-people of the highest level...
-BILL: Yeah--

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:30.944
...in comedy, make them laugh.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:32.845
So, I heard that
in the documentary,

00:03:32.911 --> 00:03:35.114
and I'm curious
if you could give me

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:36.181
one instance of that,

00:03:36.248 --> 00:03:38.484
that I can picture
a 16-year-old--

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:39.552
What did you say?

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:42.621
What did you do that made
these comedy lions laugh?

00:03:42.688 --> 00:03:45.557
Well, I did a bit once
for him and Mel

00:03:45.624 --> 00:03:47.292
-and a lot of other comedians.
-BILL: A bit?

00:03:47.359 --> 00:03:48.894
-A bit.
-Yeah, well, he came--

00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:50.263
I would come over to their house

00:03:50.329 --> 00:03:51.330
-and do bits.
-He came up with a--

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:52.531
-BILL: Really?
-On the top of his head.

00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:53.733
He didn't plan it,

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:57.803
and he just came up and he said,
"You know, I've got this thing.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:00.306
I'm the greatest escape artist
in the world.

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:05.311
I can get out of anything."
And so we took a napkin,

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:07.779
and he says, "Tie my hands up."
And I draped the napkin

00:04:07.846 --> 00:04:09.782
over his hands.
He said, "That's good enough.

00:04:09.848 --> 00:04:10.983
I can't get out of that.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:12.751
-I can't get out of that."
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:04:12.851 --> 00:04:17.123
And then he took a tissue
and he stuffed it in his mouth.

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:18.323
And he said, "Okay."

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:20.926
And then he went
behind a curtain, and he said

00:04:20.993 --> 00:04:22.661
he was gonna get out
from behind a curtain

00:04:22.728 --> 00:04:25.230
with this, and we hear
from behind the curtain,

00:04:25.297 --> 00:04:27.766
it's rustling.
We're hearing, "I can't breathe!

00:04:27.833 --> 00:04:29.035
I can't breathe!

00:04:29.101 --> 00:04:30.903
-I can't breathe! Open the--"
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

00:04:31.036 --> 00:04:33.005
We open the curtain
