-(AUDIENCE LAUGHING, APPLAUDING)

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:43.416
BILL: So, you...

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.752
-So, you were--
-Not bad for 15.

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:47.920
BILL:
No, I-- Amazing, I mean...

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:50.222
Yeah, no, no.
He was a genius and is a genius.

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:52.492
Right. Right. And wound up
doing your stand-up career

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:54.660
the same way,
even on television. Right?

00:04:54.726 --> 00:04:56.728
Not really thinking about it
before you--

00:04:56.795 --> 00:05:01.133
Well, I would work it out
by myself at home.

00:05:01.266 --> 00:05:03.002 line:0%
-BILL: Right.
-And then I would go down

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:04.971 line:0%
and I would do
national television.

00:05:05.037 --> 00:05:06.472 line:0%
I never went to a club.

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:07.573 line:0%
-Ever.
-BILL: Right

00:05:07.639 --> 00:05:08.841
Until I had done, like,

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:10.910
five years
of national television.

00:05:10.977 --> 00:05:13.012
-ROB: Yeah. It was amazing.
-So, I never tried out anything.

00:05:13.079 --> 00:05:15.981
And it was fine. It worked out.

00:05:16.048 --> 00:05:18.417
Yeah, I mean, Chris Rock says
in the documentary, he says,

00:05:18.484 --> 00:05:22.154
the idea of somebody
going on national television

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:23.655
and not even trying it out,

00:05:23.722 --> 00:05:25.023
not even seeing
if it would work,

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:26.091
That's what he did.

00:05:26.191 --> 00:05:28.193
He did it all the time.
He went on Carson 30 times.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:29.595
And he just tried up new stuff.

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:31.531
And so, by the time
you graduated high school,

00:05:31.597 --> 00:05:32.765
you were fast friends.

00:05:32.831 --> 00:05:33.833
-Yeah.
-Yeah. Yeah, yeah.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.334
Yeah.
We'd do summer stock together.

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:38.471
And then what was the--
I'm curious about the time,

00:05:38.738 --> 00:05:42.007
